1
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:06,272
All these years,
the Ministry has been concealing

2
00:00:06,573 --> 00:00:10,076
the illegal use of grants
by Seirin University Hospital?!

3
00:00:10,477 --> 00:00:13,913
Director Kikuchi of
Seirin University Hospital and

4
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:18,184
Minister Sakuragi are confidants.

5
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:23,356
I believe the minister intended
to keep it concealed.

6
00:00:24,824 --> 00:00:27,027
You were his secretary.

7
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:29,362
Why make such an accusation now?

8
00:00:29,929 --> 00:00:33,767
My doctor told me that I have cancer.

9
00:00:35,902 --> 00:00:39,539
An extrahepatic growth-type
hepatocellular carcinoma.

10
00:00:40,774 --> 00:00:41,775
Stage 4A.

11
00:00:43,176 --> 00:00:46,579
The stage is beyond
any curative surgery.

12
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:52,152
Can I allow myself to die?

13
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:57,991
Can I leave justice unrevealed
as I close the curtain of my life?

14
00:00:59,926 --> 00:01:04,431
I asked myself again and again.

15
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:08,034
It's my unwavering decision.

16
00:01:09,969 --> 00:01:13,073
Whatever time is left for me,

17
00:01:13,139 --> 00:01:16,576
I'll stick to my beliefs until the end.

18
00:01:16,976 --> 00:01:19,345
My determination is to
carry out justice.

19
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:23,183
So the Ministry has been
concealing this for years...

20
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:26,352
This is getting interesting.

21
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:34,060
Stage 4A hepatocellular carcinoma.

22
00:01:34,127 --> 00:01:36,529
Akira, go and get the job for me.

23
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,098
Not this one.

24
00:01:38,164 --> 00:01:42,535
You're bound to get involved
in the troublesome world of politics.

25
00:01:43,503 --> 00:01:47,073
Why didn't he say it
when he was in the office?

26
00:01:47,173 --> 00:01:49,509
You can't say it if you're inside,

27
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:52,512
you'll be crushed right away.

28
00:01:52,579 --> 00:01:53,713
Organizations are like that.

29
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:57,884
Whoever accuses, whether inside or not,
will be crushed.

30
00:01:57,951 --> 00:01:59,419
Even after they quit?

31
00:01:59,552 --> 00:02:02,021
Look at this article.

32
00:02:02,155 --> 00:02:03,089
See?

33
00:02:03,656 --> 00:02:07,260
Ex-secretary Yakumo's hidden life.

34
00:02:07,327 --> 00:02:09,729
His frequent visits to a baby pub.

35
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,097
A baby pub?!

36
00:02:11,231 --> 00:02:14,501
Amazingly, this came out on the
very day of the press conference.

37
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:16,603
Whoever leaked it,

38
00:02:16,669 --> 00:02:18,438
it's a smear campaign.

39
00:02:18,571 --> 00:02:23,576
Such a close relationship of
media and authority. Scary.

40
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:27,180
What is a baby pub?
What's it like?

41
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:29,782
Oh, Michiko.

42
00:02:30,016 --> 00:02:30,884
Gross.

43
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:33,820
Mommy, it's a "ron."

44
00:02:34,787 --> 00:02:38,625
"Daisushi" and "yakuman."

45
00:02:39,859 --> 00:02:42,795
Akira is such a good boy.

46
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:44,898
- Goo goo gaa gaa.
- Again?

47
00:02:45,431 --> 00:02:46,499
Goo goo gaa gaa.

48
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:47,800
This one, too?

49
00:02:49,936 --> 00:02:53,206
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

50
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,544
Excuse me! Wait for me!

51
00:02:57,610 --> 00:02:58,444
Sorry.

52
00:03:04,117 --> 00:03:05,418
<i>In 2017</i>

53
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:11,024
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

54
00:03:11,758 --> 00:03:17,797
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

55
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:24,604
- Excuse me!
- Welcome to Totei University Hospital.

56
00:03:25,772 --> 00:03:29,475
We were impressed by
your righteousness.

57
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:33,246
We'll provide you with
the best treatment.

58
00:03:35,081 --> 00:03:38,318
I'm a rebel against the Ministry,

59
00:03:39,285 --> 00:03:44,691
I didn't think there'd ever be
a hospital on my side.

60
00:03:45,124 --> 00:03:46,059
I appreciate it.

61
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:54,500
Save the life of a man
who wants justice in the world.

62
00:03:54,867 --> 00:03:57,904
This is what is called "justice."

63
00:03:59,606 --> 00:04:02,976
All of you, give him the best treatment.

64
00:04:03,042 --> 00:04:04,077
Yes sir!

65
00:04:05,278 --> 00:04:06,913
A little too tight. It hurts.

66
00:04:07,347 --> 00:04:11,884
<i>In the midst of this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

67
00:04:12,318 --> 00:04:16,823
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

68
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:20,426
I don't think we should use
a patient for advertisement.

69
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:25,064
Think of the publicity we'll get
for curing the minister's ex-secretary.

70
00:04:25,131 --> 00:04:25,965
Surely.

71
00:04:26,866 --> 00:04:27,834
But then,

72
00:04:28,134 --> 00:04:30,603
an extrahepatic growth-type
hepatocellular carcinoma.

73
00:04:31,004 --> 00:04:33,406
I'm not sure we can cure it.

74
00:04:33,473 --> 00:04:36,242
It's going to be pretty difficult.

75
00:04:38,745 --> 00:04:39,879
Please wait.

76
00:04:42,248 --> 00:04:43,082
Yes sir.

77
00:04:55,328 --> 00:04:59,365
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

78
00:04:59,866 --> 00:05:05,305
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

79
00:05:07,407 --> 00:05:09,208
Please take the next one.

80
00:05:10,376 --> 00:05:11,210
Why?

81
00:05:21,788 --> 00:05:25,258
He's Chairman Uchikanda of
Japan Doctors Club, right?

82
00:05:26,025 --> 00:05:28,094
Why is he here?

83
00:05:28,695 --> 00:05:31,230
He has a strong presence.

84
00:05:34,934 --> 00:05:36,336
Are you Ms. Daimon?

85
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:38,438
Who are you?

86
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:39,939
Watch your language.

87
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:42,909
This is Chairman Uchikanda
of Japan Doctors Club.

88
00:05:44,977 --> 00:05:46,446
You part-timer.

89
00:05:46,579 --> 00:05:47,880
Freelance.

90
00:05:48,614 --> 00:05:49,816
Michiko Daimon.

91
00:05:51,117 --> 00:05:52,785
I've heard a lot about you.

92
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:57,056
Keep doing your best.

93
00:06:05,098 --> 00:06:06,399
See you.

94
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:21,647
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

95
00:06:22,582 --> 00:06:23,850
<i>Also known as...</i>

96
00:06:24,117 --> 00:06:25,785
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

97
00:06:57,383 --> 00:06:59,719
Where is Dr. Hara?

98
00:07:00,119 --> 00:07:01,320
He's heartbroken so he's taking a trip.

99
00:07:01,988 --> 00:07:03,189
The girl he met in Russia?

100
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:05,992
Yeah, they were supposed to
go to Mount Fuji together.

101
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:09,962
I hope he's not planning to
commit suicide there.

102
00:07:11,631 --> 00:07:12,665
Oh, no.

103
00:07:13,065 --> 00:07:15,902
Let us begin
this week's pre-op conference.

104
00:07:16,702 --> 00:07:17,770
First case.

105
00:07:18,304 --> 00:07:21,073
54 years old. Male. Takuya Yakumo.

106
00:07:21,641 --> 00:07:24,544
A 9-cm tumor around
the lower central liver.

107
00:07:24,877 --> 00:07:27,313
The result of endoscopic biopsy is

108
00:07:27,847 --> 00:07:30,216
hepatocellular carcinoma
doubled with gallbladder cancer.

109
00:07:30,416 --> 00:07:31,584
As you know

110
00:07:32,018 --> 00:07:34,887
Mr. Yakumo is now at the
center of national controversy.

111
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:39,225
It's not an exaggeration to say that
the public's attention's on us.

112
00:07:39,425 --> 00:07:40,893
Not a single mistake is allowed.

113
00:07:41,327 --> 00:07:43,529
Please work on his treatment
with your utmost care.

114
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:45,031
Yes sir!

115
00:07:47,099 --> 00:07:50,303
The boundary between the tumor
and the gallbladder is unclear.

116
00:07:50,770 --> 00:07:54,841
It's a collision tumor of hepatoma
and gallbladder cancers.

117
00:07:55,441 --> 00:07:57,910
A very rare case with
many uncertain factors.

118
00:07:58,044 --> 00:07:59,111
Collision tumor.

119
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:03,015
The problem is who will be the surgeon.

120
00:08:03,249 --> 00:08:06,152
Only one person can do it.

121
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:26,739
Daimon, what would you do?

122
00:08:27,874 --> 00:08:30,276
Partial hepatectomy
and cholecystectomy.

123
00:08:30,409 --> 00:08:33,145
Remove the liver segments
S4a, S5 and S6 with

124
00:08:33,279 --> 00:08:35,615
extrahepatic tumors
including the gallbladder.

125
00:08:38,651 --> 00:08:40,786
What about the portal vein?

126
00:08:42,321 --> 00:08:44,924
Expose the left branch
while dissecting and ligating

127
00:08:45,291 --> 00:08:46,592
the caudate lobe of the portal vein.

128
00:08:52,331 --> 00:08:57,470
How about the risk of the tumor
remaining in the main portal vein?

129
00:09:00,606 --> 00:09:05,745
Remove it and reconstruct the main portal
vein by connecting it to the left branch.

130
00:09:10,149 --> 00:09:11,317
Excuse me.

131
00:09:11,417 --> 00:09:14,620
What about the resection line?

132
00:09:14,754 --> 00:09:16,255
I don't know until I cut it.

133
00:09:16,656 --> 00:09:17,757
You'll decide on the spot?

134
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:18,858
Yes.

135
00:09:18,991 --> 00:09:20,993
In other words,
be flexible and play it by ear.

136
00:09:24,664 --> 00:09:27,867
It's like a decent conference
at a good hospital.

137
00:09:27,934 --> 00:09:28,801
Huh? What is this?

138
00:09:29,035 --> 00:09:29,902
Yes.

139
00:09:31,037 --> 00:09:33,606
Please let me perform
this operation.

140
00:09:35,608 --> 00:09:37,310
Hey, Nishiyama.

141
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:38,511
Can you handle it?

142
00:09:39,178 --> 00:09:40,413
You can't handle it.

143
00:09:41,113 --> 00:09:42,148
She is right.

144
00:09:42,748 --> 00:09:46,552
This operation requires
the highest level of technique.

145
00:09:47,153 --> 00:09:49,855
Daimon, you're the only one
who can do this.

146
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:53,159
Give her your cooperation.

147
00:09:53,359 --> 00:09:55,528
Let's all work together
and save Mr. Yakumo.

148
00:09:56,696 --> 00:09:57,830
Yes sir.

149
00:09:58,731 --> 00:09:59,699
Yes sir!

150
00:10:04,036 --> 00:10:05,504
What's this sense of unity?

151
00:10:06,839 --> 00:10:08,608
I'm scared Dr. Hara...

152
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:25,124
I heard Mr. Yakumo
will have treatment here.

153
00:10:25,224 --> 00:10:28,227
Yes, I believe you'll be happy with it.

154
00:10:28,527 --> 00:10:32,431
It is going to be the operation
for the sake of justice.

155
00:10:37,937 --> 00:10:39,605
Hiruma!

156
00:10:45,277 --> 00:10:50,616
Is there something inappropriate
about this?

157
00:10:50,716 --> 00:10:53,319
Director Kikuchi of
Seirin University Hospital

158
00:10:53,386 --> 00:10:56,188
and Minister Sakuragi are friends.

159
00:10:58,524 --> 00:11:01,027
Who is the minister's friend?

160
00:11:01,727 --> 00:11:03,396
The minister's friend?

161
00:11:05,531 --> 00:11:07,166
- Who?
- I am.

162
00:11:09,068 --> 00:11:11,437
A friend of a friend is a friend.

163
00:11:11,704 --> 00:11:16,042
Many other friends will have trouble
if he talks too much.

164
00:11:17,643 --> 00:11:22,214
Mr. Yakumo made enemies out
of the whole nation.

165
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,086
Even if his life is saved,

166
00:11:29,021 --> 00:11:30,690
there won't be
anything good for him.

167
00:11:33,993 --> 00:11:35,795
Don't make me say anymore.

168
00:11:40,032 --> 00:11:42,635
I want to eat a good steak.

169
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:48,808
Read between the lines...

170
00:11:49,075 --> 00:11:53,279
I'll read between the lines for sure...

171
00:11:55,748 --> 00:11:57,049
Excuse me.

172
00:12:01,587 --> 00:12:04,390
The surgeon will be

173
00:12:04,924 --> 00:12:06,592
"I never fail" Daimon.

174
00:12:06,992 --> 00:12:07,860
I see.

175
00:12:08,227 --> 00:12:11,997
There's a high possibility that
she can cure the patient.

176
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:16,635
I'm sure he can be
summoned to the Diet.

177
00:12:16,802 --> 00:12:18,170
Hmm, I suppose so.

178
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:21,340
Under the circumstances, we'll overlook
the fact that she's a part-timer.

179
00:12:21,474 --> 00:12:24,410
Our decision is based on
executing justice as the top priority.

180
00:12:24,543 --> 00:12:25,578
Wonderful.

181
00:12:26,345 --> 00:12:27,580
Thank you.

182
00:12:28,013 --> 00:12:31,016
We are sure
you would be happy about it.

183
00:12:33,052 --> 00:12:34,220
Is this crab good?

184
00:12:34,453 --> 00:12:35,988
Yes, it is...

185
00:12:36,055 --> 00:12:36,989
Good.

186
00:12:37,890 --> 00:12:39,558
But...

187
00:12:41,627 --> 00:12:44,430
Is there anything you don't like?

188
00:12:44,563 --> 00:12:45,431
No.

189
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,735
If justice is the top priority

190
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:55,474
you shouldn't rely on
that part-timer for everything.

191
00:12:57,977 --> 00:13:01,113
You represent our Surgery Department.

192
00:13:02,581 --> 00:13:04,116
Shouldn't one of you

193
00:13:04,984 --> 00:13:06,886
perform the surgery?

194
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:17,797
I see. You mean as usual?

195
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,899
What is as usual?

196
00:13:20,032 --> 00:13:23,736
We announce one of us
is the surgeon for the operation,

197
00:13:23,803 --> 00:13:25,805
but it's Daimon who actually does it.

198
00:13:26,105 --> 00:13:27,473
Yes sir.

199
00:13:28,941 --> 00:13:29,942
Ta...

200
00:13:30,743 --> 00:13:31,877
ka...

201
00:13:32,378 --> 00:13:33,345
shi...

202
00:13:33,913 --> 00:13:36,215
All of you are a Takashi.

203
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:40,986
Hey!

204
00:13:42,388 --> 00:13:45,858
Don't let her perform the operation.

205
00:13:51,130 --> 00:13:51,997
Yes sir.

206
00:13:52,898 --> 00:13:53,933
Excuse me.

207
00:13:54,633 --> 00:13:55,835
Sorry.

208
00:13:59,638 --> 00:14:00,472
And

209
00:14:01,574 --> 00:14:03,275
the part-timer Michiko Daimon,

210
00:14:04,410 --> 00:14:06,011
don't you ever let her in the OR.

211
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:09,048
Yes sir.

212
00:14:10,716 --> 00:14:11,750
Excuse me.

213
00:14:15,354 --> 00:14:16,222
Director Hiruma.

214
00:14:17,489 --> 00:14:22,061
But if she is not the surgeon,
the patient will die.

215
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:26,899
Don't say such horrible things.

216
00:14:26,999 --> 00:14:27,833
I'm sorry.

217
00:14:28,133 --> 00:14:30,069
- You're a surgeon, right?
- Yes.

218
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:34,540
Two Takashis are gone.

219
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:36,342
So Ebina,

220
00:14:37,009 --> 00:14:40,246
you're going to perform the operation.

221
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:43,749
- No, not me.
- Why?

222
00:14:44,683 --> 00:14:46,185
- Sorry.
- That's no way to respond.

223
00:14:46,252 --> 00:14:47,353
Will you do it?

224
00:14:52,491 --> 00:14:54,260
- Well, yes sir.
- Well?

225
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,395
What do you mean?

226
00:14:56,829 --> 00:14:57,763
Don't say "Well, yes sir."

227
00:14:58,731 --> 00:14:59,765
Yes sir!

228
00:15:00,165 --> 00:15:01,033
Wow!

229
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:06,805
Why can't I be his surgeon?

230
00:15:08,307 --> 00:15:10,309
What's your plan for lymphadenectomy?

231
00:15:11,877 --> 00:15:15,547
Remove the clump including the ones
in the hepatoduodenal ligament,

232
00:15:15,681 --> 00:15:16,682
What about hemostasis?

233
00:15:18,851 --> 00:15:20,586
Block intermittently by bulldog clamp.

234
00:15:20,853 --> 00:15:22,821
Then, how do you prevent bile leaks?

235
00:15:24,523 --> 00:15:26,392
Well, let me see...

236
00:15:26,692 --> 00:15:27,860
Too slow!

237
00:15:30,663 --> 00:15:31,563
Daimon.

238
00:15:32,364 --> 00:15:35,734
I'm afraid you can't perform
the operation.

239
00:15:35,801 --> 00:15:36,869
- Why?
- What?

240
00:15:37,036 --> 00:15:39,338
- Who's going to be the surgeon?
- Dr. Ebina.

241
00:15:40,139 --> 00:15:41,140
No kidding.

242
00:15:42,841 --> 00:15:44,109
Mr. Yakumo gave his consent.

243
00:15:44,243 --> 00:15:45,277
Why?

244
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:47,479
No idea. That's it.

245
00:15:49,048 --> 00:15:50,015
Dr. Daimon.

246
00:15:52,918 --> 00:15:55,754
Things started to change after
the chairman's visit, huh?

247
00:15:55,888 --> 00:15:58,457
It's getting a bit scary, isn't it?

248
00:16:02,695 --> 00:16:03,629
Excuse me.

249
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:04,797
Daimon.

250
00:16:04,897 --> 00:16:05,898
Hi, Daimon.

251
00:16:06,398 --> 00:16:09,935
He is an important patient.
The future of Japan depends on him.

252
00:16:10,069 --> 00:16:14,640
A part-timer like you shouldn't
enter without a permission.

253
00:16:14,707 --> 00:16:16,575
- Part-timer?
- Freelance.

254
00:16:17,242 --> 00:16:19,578
Let me perform your operation.

255
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:21,213
Operation?

256
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,515
We already decided on your surgeon.

257
00:16:23,582 --> 00:16:26,452
Professor Ebina from our hospital.

258
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:27,886
Professor.

259
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:30,556
If I don't perform your operation,
you will die.

260
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:33,425
- Die?
- What are you talking about?

261
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:35,160
Why? I'm telling the truth.

262
00:16:35,227 --> 00:16:36,261
Daimon!

263
00:16:36,562 --> 00:16:37,396
Michiko Daimon!

264
00:16:38,197 --> 00:16:41,600
You have just violated
a major compliance rule.

265
00:16:43,035 --> 00:16:46,038
As the director, I'm giving an order.

266
00:16:46,972 --> 00:16:48,440
- You are fired.
- Fired?

267
00:16:48,574 --> 00:16:49,441
Hey, get her out.

268
00:16:50,309 --> 00:16:51,143
Get her out of here!

269
00:16:51,210 --> 00:16:54,980
If I'm not the surgeon, you'll die.

270
00:16:55,381 --> 00:16:56,215
Do you understand?

271
00:16:56,615 --> 00:16:58,550
It hurts! My arm!

272
00:16:58,617 --> 00:16:59,985
Look at my eyes.

273
00:17:00,052 --> 00:17:01,286
I'm going to die?

274
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:03,389
You are not going to die.

275
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:05,124
Stop it!

276
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:09,328
Daimon, please.

277
00:17:09,461 --> 00:17:10,529
Scary face.

278
00:17:10,629 --> 00:17:11,864
Please, please.

279
00:17:15,768 --> 00:17:16,668
Dr. Daimon.

280
00:17:18,103 --> 00:17:21,306
Can I talk to you now?

281
00:17:27,846 --> 00:17:29,748
About how to prevent bile leak.

282
00:17:31,083 --> 00:17:32,484
I'll use ICG.

283
00:17:33,118 --> 00:17:34,987
I'll plug leaks with fibrin glue.

284
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,222
I see.

285
00:17:38,757 --> 00:17:41,427
What is the next step

286
00:17:41,994 --> 00:17:45,164
if I can't control the bleeding
after hemostasis?

287
00:17:47,132 --> 00:17:48,434
Why should I tell you?

288
00:17:49,668 --> 00:17:52,771
I'll perform Mr. Yakumo's operation.

289
00:17:55,307 --> 00:17:57,810
I don't think Dr. Ebina can handle this.

290
00:17:58,944 --> 00:17:59,778
And yet...

291
00:18:02,014 --> 00:18:03,682
What on earth is this hospital?

292
00:18:06,118 --> 00:18:08,120
This hospital is rotten.

293
00:18:10,989 --> 00:18:12,091
So?

294
00:18:14,893 --> 00:18:16,295
I'm a doctor, too!

295
00:18:17,529 --> 00:18:18,864
I want to save lives.

296
00:18:22,067 --> 00:18:25,504
I'll pursue any means
to save patients' lives.

297
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:43,822
Director Hiruma!

298
00:18:45,891 --> 00:18:47,626
What in the world is this?!

299
00:18:51,864 --> 00:18:53,999
What the hell is this?

300
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:03,108
Dr. Morimoto, look.

301
00:19:05,777 --> 00:19:07,012
Condemnation?

302
00:19:08,413 --> 00:19:12,451
"To date, part-timer
Michiko Daimon performed

303
00:19:12,518 --> 00:19:16,221
all of the difficult operations
at Totei University Hospital

304
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:18,824
but the hospital kept it concealed."

305
00:19:18,891 --> 00:19:20,058
They found out the truth.

306
00:19:20,726 --> 00:19:21,560
What? Really?

307
00:19:21,860 --> 00:19:24,530
If you don't want this fact
to be released to the media,

308
00:19:24,963 --> 00:19:29,501
let Michiko Daimon perform
Mr. Yakumo's surgery.

309
00:19:29,801 --> 00:19:30,636
So it says.

310
00:19:30,769 --> 00:19:32,771
It's not a condemnation.

311
00:19:33,739 --> 00:19:34,573
It's blackmail.

312
00:19:36,275 --> 00:19:37,142
What's going on?

313
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:40,045
Dr. Ebina, this is a big problem!

314
00:19:42,447 --> 00:19:43,782
It's a whistleblowing.

315
00:19:44,616 --> 00:19:47,152
Who sent this?!

316
00:19:47,319 --> 00:19:48,253
I don't know.

317
00:20:18,450 --> 00:20:19,952
Ben Casey.

318
00:20:20,619 --> 00:20:24,957
Hospital fire Michiko,
babble babble...

319
00:20:25,157 --> 00:20:28,227
No surgery for Michiko,
babble babble...

320
00:20:28,293 --> 00:20:34,499
Michiko, you okay?
Me worried, babble babble...

321
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:36,768
Stop talking like a baby!

322
00:20:36,835 --> 00:20:39,738
Oh, that's scary.

323
00:20:44,776 --> 00:20:47,579
This is Kanbara Locum Doctor Agency.

324
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:52,050
Director Hiruma.
Please excuse my voice.

325
00:20:52,517 --> 00:20:53,452
You know

326
00:20:54,052 --> 00:20:59,191
did you write this, melon man?

327
00:20:59,524 --> 00:21:00,692
Let me take a look at it.

328
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,794
CONDEMNATION

329
00:21:02,861 --> 00:21:04,162
THE HOSPITAL CONCEALED...

330
00:21:04,363 --> 00:21:05,197
What's this?

331
00:21:06,365 --> 00:21:07,666
Director Hiruma,

332
00:21:08,333 --> 00:21:10,702
don't you slight me.

333
00:21:11,837 --> 00:21:15,674
To begin with,
will I benefit from doing this?

334
00:21:15,741 --> 00:21:17,509
Yeah, you are right.

335
00:21:18,644 --> 00:21:21,013
So Michiko Daimon,

336
00:21:21,346 --> 00:21:25,717
did you do this in revenge
for getting fired?

337
00:21:25,851 --> 00:21:26,752
Are you stupid?

338
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:29,888
She isn't that smart.

339
00:21:31,757 --> 00:21:34,359
Can I ask you a question?

340
00:21:34,426 --> 00:21:35,260
What?

341
00:21:35,427 --> 00:21:40,766
Did it suddenly become
inconvenient for you

342
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:44,536
if she performs
Mr. Yakumo's operation?

343
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:48,607
No, nothing but...

344
00:21:48,674 --> 00:21:49,541
Excuse me.

345
00:21:52,911 --> 00:21:54,579
Hello, this is Hiruma.

346
00:21:55,113 --> 00:21:56,315
Director Hiruma!

347
00:21:57,082 --> 00:21:57,916
Director Hiruma!

348
00:21:57,983 --> 00:21:59,351
Be quiet!

349
00:21:59,951 --> 00:22:02,354
I'm sorry. Right now...

350
00:22:03,121 --> 00:22:06,892
Ah, yes. I understand.

351
00:22:07,759 --> 00:22:09,194
Ebina, what?

352
00:22:09,394 --> 00:22:11,830
Nishiyama started
Mr. Yakumo's operation.

353
00:22:12,597 --> 00:22:13,565
That idiot!

354
00:22:13,699 --> 00:22:14,800
Hey, hey, Daimon.

355
00:22:15,367 --> 00:22:17,402
Dr. Daimon. Wait.

356
00:22:17,703 --> 00:22:20,839
I want to ask you a favor.

357
00:22:26,578 --> 00:22:27,679
OPERATING

358
00:22:27,746 --> 00:22:28,714
Collision tumor case.

359
00:22:28,780 --> 00:22:32,150
Executing partial hepatectomy
and cholecystectomy.

360
00:22:32,250 --> 00:22:33,518
Yes.

361
00:22:34,052 --> 00:22:34,886
Scalpel.

362
00:22:47,299 --> 00:22:51,770
Hey, Nishiyama! Stop it!
You can't handle this.

363
00:22:53,004 --> 00:22:54,473
I have permission from the boss.

364
00:22:54,539 --> 00:22:55,607
Monopolar.

365
00:22:55,741 --> 00:22:56,842
Who is the boss?

366
00:22:57,275 --> 00:22:59,144
We didn't give you permission!

367
00:22:59,711 --> 00:23:00,846
Hey, Nishiyama!

368
00:23:02,247 --> 00:23:03,382
Are you sure you have permission?

369
00:23:03,949 --> 00:23:04,783
Don't worry.

370
00:23:04,916 --> 00:23:06,451
Give me a break.

371
00:23:06,518 --> 00:23:08,587
You said you have permission.

372
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,755
Don't worry.

373
00:23:12,157 --> 00:23:13,058
Nishiyama!

374
00:23:21,266 --> 00:23:22,501
Vitals, please.

375
00:23:23,001 --> 00:23:26,438
BP 110 over 65.
Pulse 71.

376
00:23:27,839 --> 00:23:29,207
Continuing hepatectomy.

377
00:23:29,274 --> 00:23:30,242
Monopolar.

378
00:23:35,447 --> 00:23:36,615
Dr. Daimon?!

379
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:41,486
Don't let her perform the operation.

380
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:42,554
Get her out of here!

381
00:23:43,688 --> 00:23:46,391
Director Hiruma gave him
permission.

382
00:23:46,825 --> 00:23:49,060
And asked Daimon to be his assistant.

383
00:23:49,428 --> 00:23:50,429
What?!

384
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:52,397
What is he saying?

385
00:23:53,365 --> 00:23:54,533
What does he want?

386
00:23:58,036 --> 00:23:59,438
Bigger than I thought.

387
00:23:59,805 --> 00:24:01,673
Robust adhesion
to the transverse colon.

388
00:24:02,407 --> 00:24:03,341
Yes.

389
00:24:03,542 --> 00:24:04,643
Change position.

390
00:24:07,746 --> 00:24:10,515
What are you doing?
Continue the hepatectomy.

391
00:24:10,882 --> 00:24:11,716
Yes.

392
00:24:18,256 --> 00:24:20,559
Why did Director Hiruma
give him permission?

393
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:23,195
I don't know.

394
00:24:25,864 --> 00:24:26,698
Traction, please.

395
00:24:27,165 --> 00:24:27,999
Okay.

396
00:24:28,767 --> 00:24:31,136
- Remove the hepatic vein. Mosquito pean.
- Yes.

397
00:24:42,781 --> 00:24:44,549
Suctioning the damaged hepatic veins.

398
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:50,455
Not good. Too much bleeding.

399
00:24:50,822 --> 00:24:52,257
This is bad.

400
00:24:56,094 --> 00:24:58,630
BP decreasing. Lower than 60.

401
00:25:07,072 --> 00:25:08,507
Nishiyama! Stop the bleeding.

402
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:09,841
Hemostatic suture.

403
00:25:10,609 --> 00:25:13,078
The patient will die this way.
Change to Daimon!

404
00:25:13,245 --> 00:25:15,881
BP 55 over 25.
Pulse 130.

405
00:25:15,947 --> 00:25:16,815
Hurry up!

406
00:25:17,649 --> 00:25:19,050
- Tupfer.
- No!

407
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:22,153
- No?
- Keep dissecting.

408
00:25:23,088 --> 00:25:24,256
Dissecting?

409
00:25:27,292 --> 00:25:29,027
He's not doing
the hemostatic suture?

410
00:25:30,028 --> 00:25:31,930
What are you going to do,
Daimon?

411
00:25:46,077 --> 00:25:46,978
Move!

412
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:48,813
Move!

413
00:25:50,348 --> 00:25:53,051
Lift the liver and apply pressure on
the inferior vena cava.

414
00:25:53,151 --> 00:25:54,019
Gauze.

415
00:25:58,657 --> 00:26:00,158
Continuing hepatectomy.

416
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:01,059
Metzen.

417
00:26:01,493 --> 00:26:02,661
What?

418
00:26:09,701 --> 00:26:12,904
Suture ligature on the vein
starting from the bottom upwards.

419
00:26:15,507 --> 00:26:16,975
From the bottom upwards?!

420
00:26:17,208 --> 00:26:18,343
Don't stop the suction!

421
00:26:18,677 --> 00:26:19,544
Yes.

422
00:26:19,911 --> 00:26:21,980
Administer FFP until RBC is ready.

423
00:26:22,247 --> 00:26:23,081
Yes.

424
00:26:32,791 --> 00:26:36,394
Completed transection of the vein branch.
Suture ligature.

425
00:26:37,095 --> 00:26:38,430
Change compression.

426
00:26:55,380 --> 00:26:56,948
Wow!

427
00:26:57,148 --> 00:26:58,583
So fast.

428
00:27:07,826 --> 00:27:10,729
BP in the 70s.
Pulse recovered to 110.

429
00:27:12,530 --> 00:27:14,833
Hemostasis completed.
Continue hepatectomy.

430
00:27:14,899 --> 00:27:15,834
Bipolar.

431
00:27:22,607 --> 00:27:24,776
We'll do partial
transverse colon resection too.

432
00:27:25,276 --> 00:27:26,645
- Okay.
- Yes.

433
00:27:31,016 --> 00:27:33,018
I must say, kudos to her.

434
00:27:34,085 --> 00:27:36,021
I hate to admit that.

435
00:27:37,155 --> 00:27:40,125
But was this really okay?

436
00:27:51,136 --> 00:27:52,837
Finished. Vitals?

437
00:27:53,104 --> 00:27:56,908
BP 115 over 78.
Pulse 66, normal sinus rhythm.

438
00:28:07,585 --> 00:28:08,420
Good job.

439
00:28:08,553 --> 00:28:10,355
Thank you, Doctor...

440
00:28:12,157 --> 00:28:13,191
Come.

441
00:28:18,296 --> 00:28:19,297
Oh no.

442
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:36,915
I don't know how you got
to perform the surgery.

443
00:28:39,217 --> 00:28:40,919
Sorry for causing you trouble.

444
00:28:40,985 --> 00:28:42,220
I didn't mean that.

445
00:28:44,823 --> 00:28:45,757
The answer.

446
00:28:47,625 --> 00:28:48,793
You haven't found it yet.

447
00:28:50,662 --> 00:28:53,631
The answer for what to do
when you can't control bleeding.

448
00:28:56,267 --> 00:28:58,703
You started the operation
without being ready.

449
00:29:01,206 --> 00:29:03,508
You can't save patients' lives
that way!

450
00:29:08,913 --> 00:29:09,881
I see.

451
00:29:16,821 --> 00:29:17,689
Um...

452
00:29:18,823 --> 00:29:22,861
Chairman Uchikanda of
Japan Doctors Club is

453
00:29:26,631 --> 00:29:27,932
my father.

454
00:29:29,634 --> 00:29:30,468
Huh?

455
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:35,273
He didn't know that.

456
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:43,281
Are you really my son?

457
00:29:45,850 --> 00:29:46,684
Yes.

458
00:29:49,587 --> 00:29:52,791
My mother was a nurse.

459
00:29:53,324 --> 00:29:55,393
She dated Surgeon Uchikanda.

460
00:29:57,595 --> 00:30:00,298
And then became pregnant with me.

461
00:30:02,834 --> 00:30:08,306
But at the same time, he was
getting married to the dean's daughter.

462
00:30:09,073 --> 00:30:10,241
It's a common story.

463
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:17,115
My mother didn't tell him
about the pregnancy and left him.

464
00:30:18,616 --> 00:30:20,151
That's what she told me.

465
00:30:21,853 --> 00:30:24,088
I guess it was her pride as a woman.

466
00:30:25,390 --> 00:30:27,058
I'm sure he dumped my mother.

467
00:30:29,561 --> 00:30:31,062
She was a single mother

468
00:30:32,096 --> 00:30:35,066
but got me into medical school.

469
00:30:37,936 --> 00:30:38,837
But...

470
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:42,173
The year I got my doctor's license...

471
00:30:45,610 --> 00:30:47,078
She had advanced breast cancer.

472
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:53,785
Kimie passed away.

473
00:30:55,687 --> 00:30:56,521
Yes.

474
00:30:57,856 --> 00:31:02,827
I was going to leak it to the media.

475
00:31:05,463 --> 00:31:08,199
But I won't do that.

476
00:31:10,201 --> 00:31:11,569
She wouldn't want me to.

477
00:31:15,473 --> 00:31:17,108
But I'd like to ask something in return.

478
00:31:19,911 --> 00:31:21,045
Mr. Yakumo's operation,

479
00:31:23,715 --> 00:31:25,049
please let me perform it.

480
00:31:30,521 --> 00:31:31,422
So?

481
00:31:38,596 --> 00:31:40,698
It's your fault, Dr. Daimon.

482
00:31:42,967 --> 00:31:44,135
Until I met you,

483
00:31:45,536 --> 00:31:48,673
I planned to blend in
within the organization.

484
00:31:49,807 --> 00:31:50,642
Of course

485
00:31:51,175 --> 00:31:55,179
I wasn't going to tell anybody
that I'm his son.

486
00:31:57,448 --> 00:31:58,283
But then,

487
00:32:00,018 --> 00:32:03,221
there's no point in me becoming a doctor.

488
00:32:08,059 --> 00:32:09,794
I watched your operations,

489
00:32:11,329 --> 00:32:12,630
and began to think this way.

490
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:18,970
I want to become a doctor

491
00:32:20,872 --> 00:32:21,706
like you.

492
00:32:22,807 --> 00:32:26,711
So I wanted to challenge
a tough surgery.

493
00:32:28,413 --> 00:32:30,114
To become a doctor who never fails,

494
00:32:31,516 --> 00:32:33,184
you may fail at times.

495
00:32:39,924 --> 00:32:40,858
You mean

496
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:47,765
you can sacrifice patients' lives
for your improvement?

497
00:32:48,032 --> 00:32:50,335
I didn't say that.

498
00:32:51,069 --> 00:32:54,439
However as a result,
there are cases.

499
00:32:54,706 --> 00:32:57,742
There is no next time for the patient.

500
00:33:00,144 --> 00:33:01,612
But there's a next time for you.

501
00:33:06,551 --> 00:33:07,719
So doctors

502
00:33:09,387 --> 00:33:11,289
should never fail.

503
00:33:32,744 --> 00:33:33,644
Excuse me.

504
00:33:35,580 --> 00:33:41,052
Thank you for employing Daimon
and Jonouchi from our agency.

505
00:33:41,252 --> 00:33:46,224
This time I thought it's appropriate
to settle the bill here.

506
00:33:46,891 --> 00:33:47,759
A melon.

507
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:52,063
The bill.

508
00:34:04,542 --> 00:34:05,376
$100,000

509
00:34:05,476 --> 00:34:09,614
Do you always rip us off
with this outrageous amount?

510
00:34:10,415 --> 00:34:12,750
It's not like you to talk that way.

511
00:34:15,086 --> 00:34:19,090
The man may put you
in a tight corner,

512
00:34:19,524 --> 00:34:21,092
but you saved his life.

513
00:34:21,926 --> 00:34:23,327
Why did you do it?

514
00:34:24,395 --> 00:34:28,699
One failure may leave a huge stain
on a doctor's reputation.

515
00:34:29,333 --> 00:34:33,071
So you ordered Director Hiruma

516
00:34:33,438 --> 00:34:37,575
to let Daimon assist Dr. Nishiyama.

517
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:40,445
Why is that?

518
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,182
You love your son.

519
00:34:46,918 --> 00:34:49,954
You're a father after all.

520
00:34:50,354 --> 00:34:51,222
Ucchy.

521
00:35:02,433 --> 00:35:04,602
You have such a big kid.

522
00:35:05,670 --> 00:35:07,872
No wonder we're getting old.

523
00:35:10,174 --> 00:35:11,242
No, it's not like that.

524
00:35:12,643 --> 00:35:15,580
I made the best choice to
save the patient.

525
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:22,120
What more reason is there
for doctors saving patients' lives?

526
00:35:24,755 --> 00:35:26,557
I'll transfer the money
to your account.

527
00:35:29,293 --> 00:35:30,761
Thank you.

528
00:35:48,579 --> 00:35:52,283
My surgery was successful?

529
00:35:52,350 --> 00:35:56,754
Yes, I can say that
it was a huge success.

530
00:35:57,121 --> 00:36:01,359
Dr. Nishiyama did his best
as your surgeon.

531
00:36:03,060 --> 00:36:06,063
I thought Dr. Ebina was the surgeon.

532
00:36:06,197 --> 00:36:11,669
Dr. Nishiyama is the young ace
at this hospital.

533
00:36:12,236 --> 00:36:16,407
I can say your cancer is cured.

534
00:36:16,807 --> 00:36:18,342
- Really?
- Yes, it's true.

535
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:22,413
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

536
00:36:26,250 --> 00:36:27,718
I really appreciate it.

537
00:36:28,653 --> 00:36:31,422
Dr. Nishiyama. Good job.

538
00:36:31,489 --> 00:36:32,757
Thank you so much.

539
00:36:32,890 --> 00:36:34,959
- I'm glad.
- Good.

540
00:36:38,696 --> 00:36:41,232
Dr. Nishiyama did a good job, indeed.

541
00:36:46,103 --> 00:36:50,041
By the best medical
technology in Japan,

542
00:36:50,841 --> 00:36:52,810
I was able to regain my life.

543
00:36:53,711 --> 00:36:54,712
Director Hiruma.

544
00:36:56,180 --> 00:36:57,148
Dr. Nishiyama.

545
00:36:58,583 --> 00:37:02,820
I appreciate the courage and
determination of you two.

546
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:04,155
Thank you.

547
00:37:04,422 --> 00:37:05,423
Thank you so much.

548
00:37:05,489 --> 00:37:08,092
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

549
00:37:12,396 --> 00:37:13,331
Mr. Yakumo.

550
00:37:13,965 --> 00:37:14,799
Yes?

551
00:37:15,066 --> 00:37:19,904
Are you going to attend the Diet
as a witness?

552
00:37:23,641 --> 00:37:26,077
I've gone over

553
00:37:26,277 --> 00:37:30,314
all the past references and documents.

554
00:37:31,082 --> 00:37:33,918
But the facts on the Ministry concealing

555
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:39,123
the illegal use of grants
by Seirin University Hospital

556
00:37:39,190 --> 00:37:41,692
could not be confirmed.

557
00:37:42,293 --> 00:37:44,061
I couldn't confirm it.

558
00:37:48,165 --> 00:37:51,202
So your accusation was a mistake?

559
00:37:52,303 --> 00:37:53,337
Yes.

560
00:37:54,572 --> 00:37:57,808
It was all due to my wrong memories.

561
00:37:58,542 --> 00:38:01,379
I'd like to take this opportunity
to apologize.

562
00:38:02,913 --> 00:38:06,751
I am really sorry.

563
00:38:21,165 --> 00:38:26,837
My goodness, a wrong memory?!
What was it all about then?

564
00:38:27,171 --> 00:38:30,908
He realized he could live longer
and therefore,

565
00:38:31,042 --> 00:38:35,379
he decided not to make waves
but yield to the powerful.

566
00:38:36,180 --> 00:38:39,984
There's a rumor the Ministry
has a post for him to parachute.

567
00:38:40,117 --> 00:38:43,654
After all, our Diet is a
pandemonium of monsters.

568
00:38:44,855 --> 00:38:46,123
I can't believe this!

569
00:38:48,125 --> 00:38:52,229
Oh, we have a monster here, too.

570
00:38:53,898 --> 00:38:55,399
What monster?

571
00:38:56,467 --> 00:39:00,571
This whistleblowing fax.

572
00:39:00,938 --> 00:39:04,375
The sender's number is
displayed here at the corner.

573
00:39:04,842 --> 00:39:06,310
Is it a number at this hospital?

574
00:39:06,377 --> 00:39:08,813
It's from the Chemical Storage.

575
00:39:08,946 --> 00:39:10,281
The Chemical Storage?!

576
00:39:10,915 --> 00:39:15,820
I borrowed a video of the security camera
from the Emergency Control Center.

577
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:18,489
The one around the time
the fax was sent.

578
00:39:20,191 --> 00:39:21,092
This is

579
00:39:22,226 --> 00:39:23,060
the video.

580
00:39:23,494 --> 00:39:28,599
CHEMICAL STORAGE

581
00:39:35,573 --> 00:39:37,074
Why Dr. Ebina?!

582
00:39:41,011 --> 00:39:43,848
Not me.
He has similar features.

583
00:39:43,981 --> 00:39:46,217
Obviously it's you.

584
00:39:46,283 --> 00:39:47,718
I deny it. It's not me.

585
00:39:50,955 --> 00:39:51,789
No.

586
00:39:51,922 --> 00:39:53,290
I'm going out for lunch.

587
00:39:53,357 --> 00:39:55,226
I'll come with you.
Let's eat steak!

588
00:39:56,460 --> 00:39:58,162
Too close. Scary.

589
00:40:00,498 --> 00:40:06,504
Maybe Dr. Ebina tried to have Daimon do it
because he can't handle it?

590
00:40:06,604 --> 00:40:10,341
I sort of understand as a doctor,
you don't want to fail, but...

591
00:40:10,674 --> 00:40:13,944
He is totally unreliable.

592
00:40:18,682 --> 00:40:19,750
It wasn't me.

593
00:40:23,254 --> 00:40:24,488
That's not the real me!

594
00:40:25,823 --> 00:40:26,757
What should I do?

595
00:40:27,224 --> 00:40:28,292
But it can't be helped.

596
00:40:32,930 --> 00:40:36,834
You attended Mr. Yakumo's
press conference, right?

597
00:40:37,968 --> 00:40:38,903
Thank you.

598
00:40:40,704 --> 00:40:42,873
I just wanted to settle
what I owe you.

599
00:40:44,008 --> 00:40:44,875
You owe me?

600
00:40:45,042 --> 00:40:48,078
I was able to operate
because of you.

601
00:40:49,713 --> 00:40:50,781
Thank you so much.

602
00:40:54,485 --> 00:40:55,653
It's strange.

603
00:40:56,821 --> 00:40:58,622
I have three sons.

604
00:40:59,723 --> 00:41:02,693
But none of them became a doctor.

605
00:41:03,194 --> 00:41:04,728
They didn't even try.

606
00:41:05,863 --> 00:41:07,064
Maybe that is why.

607
00:41:07,665 --> 00:41:11,769
When you showed up,
I was very happy.

608
00:41:14,905 --> 00:41:16,273
Even though you threatened me.

609
00:41:27,718 --> 00:41:28,886
Your watch.

610
00:41:29,386 --> 00:41:30,921
I left it at
Kimie's place.

611
00:41:31,722 --> 00:41:32,656
It was mine.

612
00:41:34,391 --> 00:41:35,426
Yes.

613
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:42,199
Time didn't stop...

614
00:41:49,773 --> 00:41:52,443
I became a doctor

615
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:56,580
because my mother supported me.

616
00:41:58,549 --> 00:42:03,988
She used to say
you are a great doctor.

617
00:42:05,990 --> 00:42:06,857
Kimie...

618
00:42:07,625 --> 00:42:08,492
Yes.

619
00:42:10,394 --> 00:42:11,228
So

620
00:42:12,563 --> 00:42:16,967
she wanted me to follow
the same path as you.

621
00:42:21,105 --> 00:42:21,972
Maybe

622
00:42:25,175 --> 00:42:30,014
I was longing to be like you.

623
00:42:34,785 --> 00:42:36,387
Surgeons need experiences.

624
00:42:37,588 --> 00:42:40,391
I'll keep supporting you
for your operations.

625
00:42:42,993 --> 00:42:44,295
Feel free to ask me a favor.

626
00:42:46,430 --> 00:42:47,598
Go ahead and eat.

627
00:43:03,547 --> 00:43:04,381
Shut up!

628
00:43:05,382 --> 00:43:09,853
You almost killed the patient!

629
00:43:11,455 --> 00:43:12,356
Do you get it?

630
00:43:13,190 --> 00:43:18,762
I don't care about your power or you.
I'm not interested.

631
00:43:19,697 --> 00:43:20,965
I don't care about the organization,

632
00:43:22,933 --> 00:43:25,502
or any authority.
They're all damn nonsense!

633
00:43:51,595 --> 00:43:55,432
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

634
00:43:56,834 --> 00:43:58,469
I'm sorry about last time.

635
00:44:00,170 --> 00:44:01,739
OR 2!

636
00:44:05,743 --> 00:44:06,577
Yes!

637
00:44:21,425 --> 00:44:22,259
Let's begin.

638
00:44:23,827 --> 00:44:24,928
Scalpel.

639
00:44:26,563 --> 00:44:28,298
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

640
00:44:29,266 --> 00:44:31,935
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>

641
00:44:32,236 --> 00:44:33,671
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

642
00:44:33,837 --> 00:44:38,876
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

643
00:44:54,324 --> 00:44:56,160
Japan Doctors Club.

644
00:44:57,594 --> 00:45:01,799
Chairman Uchikanda's son...

645
00:45:10,641 --> 00:45:11,742
Metzen.

646
00:45:18,348 --> 00:45:20,718
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

647
00:45:21,051 --> 00:45:22,186
<i>Also known as...</i>

648
00:45:22,686 --> 00:45:24,455
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

649
00:45:29,526 --> 00:45:31,261
I'm terminating the freelancers!

650
00:45:31,395 --> 00:45:33,330
Ruin the patient's future?!

651
00:45:33,464 --> 00:45:35,365
Be the principal dancer.

652
00:45:35,432 --> 00:45:36,500
A screw made of bone.

653
00:45:36,567 --> 00:45:37,935
Suspension of business?

654
00:45:38,001 --> 00:45:40,604
Uchikanda, you're making a mistake.

655
00:45:41,171 --> 00:45:42,773
Dr. Daimon.
